<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LanguageData>
  
  <!-- EN: Additional Armor Plating -->
  <DMS_BF_ExtendArmor.label>附加装甲</DMS_BF_ExtendArmor.label>
  <!-- EN: Composite armor plates designed for battle frame pylons add survivability to the battle frame by protecting it from fragmentation and medium-caliber gunfire. -->
  <DMS_BF_ExtendArmor.description>一种安装在战斗框架侧面挂架的复合装甲板，可有效抵御破片与中小口径枪械的直接射击并保护其动力部位不受损伤。</DMS_BF_ExtendArmor.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_BF_ExtendArmor.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_BF_ExtendArmor.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: Extended Cargo Rack -->
  <DMS_BF_ExtendCargo.label>加挂货箱</DMS_BF_ExtendCargo.label>
  <!-- EN: Side mounted cargo racks suitable for battle frame pylons. The racks increase the carrying capacity of battle frame and their variants. -->
  <DMS_BF_ExtendCargo.description>一种安装在战斗框架侧面挂架的金属箱，通常被用於山地区域的长途运输与前线补给小队用来提高运输效率。</DMS_BF_ExtendCargo.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_BF_ExtendCargo.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_BF_ExtendCargo.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: Recoilless Rifle Rack -->
  <DMS_BF_RecoillessRifle.label>无后座力炮挂架</DMS_BF_RecoillessRifle.label>
  <!-- EN: A pair of 65mm recoilless tubes on a shared cradle, built to bolt onto the side pylons of a battle frame. Line units fit it for one reason: a frame's own light armament has no answer to plating or a prepared firing position, and a walking mount can carry the tube into ground a two-man crew would never reach.\n\nLoaded with shaped-charge rockets, the rack defeats armor and fortifications far above the frame's weight class, and its fire control unit reloads a spent tube from carried stores between engagements. The frame pays for it in walking pace, dodging room and cargo allowance, and every backblast marks its position for every observer on the field. -->
  <DMS_BF_RecoillessRifle.description>一组安装在战斗框架侧面挂点的双联装65mm无后座力炮摇架。前线单位加挂它的理由很单纯：框架自身的轻型武装对装甲载具与构工阵地毫无办法，而会走路的载台能把炮管带进双人炮组永远到不了的地形。\n\n装填聚能穿甲火箭后，挂架能击穿远超框架自身量级的装甲与工事，射控单元会在交战间隙从自携弹药中重新装填空管。代价是框架的步速、闪避余裕与载运能力同时下降，而且每一次后喷焰都会把它的位置标示给战场上所有观测器材。</DMS_BF_RecoillessRifle.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_BF_RecoillessRifle.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_BF_RecoillessRifle.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: broken ceramics -->
  <DMS_BrokenCeramics.label>破碎陶瓷</DMS_BrokenCeramics.label>
  
  <!-- EN: Ceramic Plates -->
  <DMS_CeramicsPlating.label>抛弃式陶瓷装甲</DMS_CeramicsPlating.label>
  <!-- EN: A set of ceramic plates designed to be mounted on to a mech's external shell to provide additional protection. Once damaged, the armor plating must be completely replaced.\n\nThe maximum amount of plating able to be installed on a mech can depends on its body size. -->
  <DMS_CeramicsPlating.description>一组抛弃式陶瓷装甲板与安装用的支架和工具组等，陶瓷装甲板可以安装在机兵的机体上以提供额外的防护，但一经损坏就只能更换新的。 \n\n最大可安装数量取决於安装机体的体型。</DMS_CeramicsPlating.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_CeramicsPlating.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_CeramicsPlating.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: Nuclear Battery -->
  <DMS_NuclearBattery.label>裂变电池</DMS_NuclearBattery.label>
  <!-- EN: A nuclear fission reactor powering a quantum battery, this device is commonly found in many unmanned signal stations and defense robots. It consists of six high-density uranium-235 columns with integrated thermocouples all wrapped in a high-strength shell. Its energy is enough to make most models of automatroid operate for decades. -->
  <DMS_NuclearBattery.description>一种结构简单的核裂变电池，常见於许多无人职守的讯号站与驻防灯塔用的机兵上，由六根接近临界质量的柱状高密度铀235与热电偶集成并包裹在一个高强度壳体中。其输出的能量足够让绝大部分型号的机兵运转长达数百年，并且在紧急情况下也可以变为一次性核弹使用。</DMS_NuclearBattery.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_NuclearBattery.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_NuclearBattery.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: Reinforced Frame -->
  <DMS_ReinforcedFrame.label>强化骨架</DMS_ReinforcedFrame.label>
  <!-- EN: A set of tungsteel parts made to replace those prone to wearing down, effectively improving reliability and durability during high-intensity combat. These heavy duty replacement parts will significantly increase the weight of the mech and affect its speed. -->
  <DMS_ReinforcedFrame.description>一系列使用钨钢合金来替换机兵骨架中较易磨损部位的强化零组件，可以有效提高在高强度战斗时的耐用性并且能在火力压制下也不受干扰的行动。但作为代价会显着提高机兵的重量并影响速度。</DMS_ReinforcedFrame.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_ReinforcedFrame.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_ReinforcedFrame.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: Synthetic Tendon -->
  <DMS_SyntheticTendon.label>合成肌腱</DMS_SyntheticTendon.label>
  <!-- EN: Biosynthetic muscles attached on the outer layer of mechanical limbs. Synthetic tendons effectively increase output at the cost of additional energy consumption. -->
  <DMS_SyntheticTendon.description>一种安装在机体腿部出力位置的人工生物合成肌腱，透过外部接口接入机体能源来进行供能，能有效的增加关节出力但同时增加能源消耗。</DMS_SyntheticTendon.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_SyntheticTendon.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_SyntheticTendon.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: Heavy Hydraulic Frame -->
  <DMS_TB_HeavyHydraulicFrame.label>重型液压框架</DMS_TB_HeavyHydraulicFrame.label>
  <!-- EN: A high durability reinforced hydraulic frame designed as a platform for mounting heavy weapons on Iguanas and Geckos. -->
  <DMS_TB_HeavyHydraulicFrame.description>一种适用於重型双足机兵的外置液压骨架和动力包，可以简单的理解为机兵专用的外骨骼系统，能使重型机兵获得更大的战斗负载容量，还可以安装超重型武器。但作为代价会显着提高机兵的重量与移动速度。</DMS_TB_HeavyHydraulicFrame.description>
  <!-- EN: Use {0_label} -->
  <DMS_TB_HeavyHydraulicFrame.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>安装{0}</DMS_TB_HeavyHydraulicFrame.comps.CompUsable.useLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: unfinished modification -->
  <UnfinishedModification.label>未完成的改装件</UnfinishedModification.label>
  <!-- EN: An unfinished modification. -->
  <UnfinishedModification.description>一个尚未完成的机兵改装组件</UnfinishedModification.description>
  
</LanguageData>